{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"So, when people ask, the game date in Arcania is 1783. But clearly we are bringing the early irl 19th century back in time. This is likely to feel more like the industrial scale of the world wars than real revolutionary war. The blend is going to be interesting. Single shot guns and ornithropters. Muskets and railroads all blended into one thing. Just a thought.","created_at":"2020-08-26T21:21:43.879000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"748291112845967401","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_rail_transport","created_at":"2020-08-29T05:35:34.458000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"749140168232927303","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"Rails were definitely around in 1783, but they were still using cast iron, which were prone to breaking. I think only having local rails would be better. Maybe the longest run would be New York to Philadelphia or some similar distance. Trains would be unreliable and prone to malfunction which is why mechanics would be so important.","created_at":"2020-08-29T05:37:28.037000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"749140644617781258","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"for the purposes of the game, its going to be like trains in a video game, they just run circles around the city.","created_at":"2020-08-29T06:04:31.269000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"749147452946251806","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"justjack420","id":"592252026226999306","is_bot":0,"username":"justjack420"},"author_id":"592252026226999306","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"Proposed Loot rules for Tales of Arcania\n\nAt the end of every weekly event players get to roll a d20 on a loot table specific to their class.\n-In the event of a multiclassed character they may choose one of the classes they have leveled into.\n-They are able to trade these items among each other as they please, so long as the PC fits any requirements needed.\n-The items on the list are arranged in rarity with a 1 being a more common, but still useful item to their class, and a 20 being a higher quality item that is massively desired.\n-Items on the list will come from DMG, XGE, and The Griffon’s Saddlebag, as well as those created specifically for Tales of Arcania.\n-Players may spend Inspiration on the loot table if they wish and choose between the two results.\n\n\nPROS\nGuaranteed loot for all participants\nMore useful loot for individuals \nNo “wasted” loot\n\nCONS\nLonger/more complex looting time\nCan’t think of more, but I’m a proponent of this idea.\n\nIf you have any thoughts, recommendations, or want to help build out the lists let me know.\n13 (Maybe 14 or 15 if we allow the Blood Hunter and have the Arbiter finished) tables are a lot to fill and I’m only well versed in a couple of the classes.","created_at":"2020-09-07T21:02:41.738000Z","edited_at":"2020-09-07T21:02:55.866000Z","id":"752634976746471504","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"I like this idea!","created_at":"2020-09-08T01:34:40.774000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"752703423744442428","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"Proposed loot chart catagories:\nStrength weapons (sub cat for size?)\nDexterity weapons (sub cat for size/range?)\nArmor\nConsumables\nScrolls (this would be a scroll of your own spell list, randomly assigned maybe?) \nYou could choose from one list of what your character is looking for while looting and then the roll would determine what you found. Then you'd also get your cut of gold. \nAnother fun idea is a magical item category of the homebrew items.\nAll of these could have sub categories of rarity if we wanted. So weekly battles hand out rarer stuff and lesser fights, more common items.","created_at":"2020-09-08T01:40:48.607000Z","edited_at":"2020-09-08T01:43:50.930000Z","id":"752704966547734699","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
